<p>The Pentagon has identified all six U.S. Army Reserve service members killed when a drone struck a command center at a U.S. military facility in Port Shuaiba, Kuwait, on Sunday. The final two names released were Maj. Jeffrey R. O’Brien and Chief Warrant Officer 3 Robert M. Marzan. The Pentagon said Marzan’s identification still needs confirmation by the medical examiner.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CY3L4C0NiWkcQhr4hn4XtWMmyAqV98-2GmbiHv_BaGaupY2dwoxIXKEad5Tu8DWtcJswDdX8lKaMzPm8dmD0WYtWdbyqpq5XKZ1e9aLclEU2h15q8KOe06E0hfQp7t2qeiLbz_Kb4gV1PyR7BNWIveeZfPfS1plrzeYiil8B0W6PQQScdVboayNe-_wXiN7zWywtw1EFkj9WgLvB5_aTPvWCcZyYf0OBJa5MyjOT5Il27kHM7OkBiSNNI0dd8Bj5TaRkUiJO6Wkf9IzoW1R0' alt='A U.S. Army Reserve-related image accompanying reporting on the Kuwait attack.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>The Pentagon named the six service members killed: Sgt. Declan Coady, Sgt. 1st Class Nicole Amor, Capt. Cody Khork, Sgt. 1st Class Noah Tietjens, Maj. Jeffrey R. O’Brien, and Chief Warrant Officer 3 Robert M. Marzan.</li><li>The last two identified were O’Brien, 45, of Indianola, Iowa, and Marzan, 54, of Sacramento, California.</li><li>In the broader conflict, The Guardian said the Kuwait attack came Sunday, a day after the U.S. and Israel launched strikes against Iran.</li><li>CBS cited U.S. Central Command, which said American service members were killed in the U.S.-Iran conflict.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Department of Defense: The Pentagon released the final two names on Wednesday and described Robert M. Marzan’s status as a “believed death,” pending positive identification by the medical examiner. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pentagon-identifies-two-soldiers-killed-iran-war'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>BBC: The BBC said the drone “evaded air defences” before hitting a command centre, calling it a major breach in protection. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq33ynl07o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>CBS News: CBS News raised questions about the Port Shuaiba site’s apparent lack of defenses, pointing to satellite imagery and describing the facility before and after the strike. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/new-details-about-facility-where-iranian-drone-strike-killed-six-us-soldiers/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The New York Times emphasized individual biographies and plans—such as a service member nearing the end of a deployment and hoping to open a martial arts studio—grounding the losses in the communities they came from. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/us-soldiers-killed-iran-war.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/soldiers-killed-kuwait'>Pentagon releases names of final two soldiers of six killed in Kuwait</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pentagon-identifies-two-soldiers-killed-iran-war'>Pentagon identifies two soldiers killed in Iran war</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/04/g-s1-112474/soldiers-killed-iran-war-kuwait-army-reserve-iowa-amor-coady-khork-tietjens'>The Pentagon has now ID&#x27;d all 6 U.S. soldiers who died in a Kuwait attack</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/us-soldiers-killed-iran-war.html'>These American Service Members Died in the Iran Conflict</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/pentagon-identifies-two-soldiers-killed-in-iran-war'>Pentagon identifies two more soldiers killed in Iran war</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq33ynl07o'>Pentagon identifies six US soldiers killed in Iran conflict</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-service-members-killed-iran-war-what-we-know/'>What we know about U.S. service members killed in Iran war</a> - cbsnews.com</li></ul>